Description: build the rdef from source/, where the file ships
 The Makefile points RDEFS at sources/armyknife.rdef while the release
 ships source/armyknife.rdef, so make stops with "No rule to make target
 'sources/armyknife.rdef'" and the binary would come out without any
 resources. Upstream master still carries the same typo.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 
 #	Specify the resource definition files to use. Full or relative paths can be
 #	used.
-RDEFS = sources/armyknife.rdef
+RDEFS = source/armyknife.rdef
 
 #	Specify the resource files to use. Full or relative paths can be used.
 #	Both RDEFS and RSRCS can be utilized in the same Makefile.
